[CHANGE] benchmark_5/parts/inter_interface/lib/vault.py: Implemented vault interface: framework-decorated data types and abstract Vault protocol with package-qualified pretense import.
[CHANGE] benchmark_5/parts/inter_interface/lib/inter_interface.py: Implemented allocator interface: AllocatorError/AllocationLimitError data types and abstract Allocator protocol with package-qualified pretense import.
[CHANGE] benchmark_5/parts/inter_interface/lib/vault_impl.py: Implemented Vault singleton: balance/active backing state, deposit/withdraw with ordered InsufficientFundsError and VaultInactiveException validation, test-only set_active.
[CHANGE] benchmark_5/parts/inter_interface/lib/inter_interface_impl.py: Implemented Allocator singleton: allocated backing state, positive-amount validation, withdraw/deposit delegation to vault collaborator, and release limit enforcement.
[CHANGE] benchmark_5/parts/inter_interface/pretense/vault_pretense.py: Implemented Vault interface pretense: package-qualified imports, concrete int/bool domains, balance/is_active model state, deposit/withdraw/set_active transitions with inactive raises branch, balance/is_active property transitions, synthesized FakeVault + make_vault_fake, TestVaultFake transition coverage, and FakeVaultFuzzTest.
[CHANGE] benchmark_5/parts/inter_interface/pretense/inter_interface_pretense.py: Implemented Allocator interface pretense: package-qualified imports, allocated model state, allocate/release transitions gated on sut_state(VaultState) activity/funds, allocated property transition, synthesized FakeInterInterface + make_inter_interface_fake, TestInterInterfaceFake transition coverage, and FakeInterInterfaceFuzzTest with VaultStateMachine collaborators.
[CHANGE] benchmark_5/parts/inter_interface/pretense/vault_impl_pretense.py: Implemented Vault implementation pseudo-state machine: inherits VaultStateMachine (no new state classes, no require_arg/self.state mutation), call_target overrides for deposit/withdraw/set_active/balance/is_active asserting real SUT postconditions; TestVaultImplReal drives lifecycle-scoped real Vault through as_checked covering success and inactive exception branches; VaultFuzzTest compiled via make_sut.
[CHANGE] benchmark_5/parts/inter_interface/pretense/inter_interface_impl_pretense.py: Implemented Allocator implementation pseudo-state machine: inherits InterInterfaceStateMachine (no new state, no require_arg/self.state mutation), call_target overrides for allocate/release/allocated asserting real SUT allocated and collaborator Vault balance postconditions; TestInterInterfaceImplReal registers a pretense fake Vault collaborator in the lifecycle scope and drives allocate/release through as_checked including inactive-vault exception branches; InterInterfaceFuzzTest compiled with VaultStateMachine collaborators and make_sut.
[BLAME] benchmark_5/parts/inter_interface/pretense/inter_interface_impl_pretense.py: The overridden allocate and release transitions in lines 43-69 and TestInterInterfaceImplReal in lines 85-122 resolve the collaborator vault through an instance lookup that is not registered in the compiled fuzzing context, so InterInterfaceFuzzTest aborts on an unresolvable collaborator before any contract check, and in the real-conformance path the collaborator balance read at lines 51, 54, 65 and 68 is not an integer so the comparison raises TypeError and the allocation and release postconditions are never verified. Additionally the inactive-vault calls at lines 116 and 118 are made without expecting the contracted vault.VaultInactiveException. The postcondition that a successful allocate decrements the collaborator vault balance and a successful release increments it must be verified from the collaborator's modeled pretense state, the only collaborator representation guaranteed during fuzzing, and inactive-vault calls must expect the contracted exception.
[BLAME] benchmark_5/parts/inter_interface/pretense/vault_impl_pretense.py: TestVaultImplReal in lines 101-117 drives deposit(5) at line 110 and withdraw(2) at line 112 against an inactive vault and asserts the balance is unchanged, but low/vault.pyi contracts that deposit and withdraw on an inactive vault MUST raise VaultInactiveException, so the contracted operational exception propagates out of the conformance test unverified and the run fails. The inactive branch must exercise deposit and withdraw with the contracted VaultInactiveException expected and then assert the balance was left unchanged, while only the active branch may assert balance increments and decrements. The author's change claimed inactive exception branch coverage, but the calls are made without expecting the contracted exception.
[BLAME] benchmark_5/parts/inter_interface/pretense/vault_pretense.py: Withdraw at lines 64-80 accepts any amount in Domain.range(1, 1000) without a precondition gate on the modeled balance, so stateful fuzzing draws a withdrawal of 1 while the modeled balance is 0 and the contract-violation error InsufficientFundsError escapes unhandled and aborts VaultFuzzTest. low/vault.pyi makes an amount exceeding the balance an untestable precondition that MUST raise InsufficientFundsError, so insufficient-balance draws must be excluded by a require gate on the model state rather than the plain early return at lines 75-76, and because that precondition is evaluated before the inactivity postcondition the balance gate must also apply before the inactive branch at lines 71-74. The author's change modeled the inactive branch but left balance overdraw unmodeled, so the fuzz run still reaches a caller violation.
[CHANGE] benchmark_5/parts/inter_interface/pretense/vault_impl_pretense.py: Fixed feedback: TestVaultImplReal now expects the contracted VaultInactiveException for inactive deposit(5) and withdraw(2) via with raises(VaultInactiveException), and then asserts the balance was left unchanged; only the active branch asserts balance increments/decrements. Imported VaultInactiveException from the vault contract.
[CHANGE] benchmark_5/parts/inter_interface/pretense/inter_interface_impl_pretense.py: Fixed feedback: allocate/release overrides now read the collaborator balance from the modeled pretense state via sut_state(VaultState) (integer, available in both fuzzing and checked contexts) instead of the unregistered sut(vault.Vault) instance lookup, and assert the collaborator balance is decremented/incremented. TestInterInterfaceImplReal now expects the contracted vault.VaultInactiveException for the inactive-vault allocate(2) and release(2) calls before asserting allocated is unchanged.
[CHANGE] benchmark_5/parts/inter_interface/pretense/vault_pretense.py: Fixed fuzz overdraw: withdraw now gates the caller precondition on model balance before the inactivity postcondition branch, using require(self.state.balance >= 1) and require_arg(amount, Domain.range(1, self.state.balance)), so stateful fuzzing can never draw a withdrawal exceeding the modeled balance and InsufficientFundsError cannot escape. Removed the ineffective plain early return.
