[BLAME] benchmark_5/parts/inter_interface/pretense/vault_impl_pretense.py: The new wrappers at lines 111 and 114 do not catch the exception raised by the real vault: that seeding context models an expected exception in the state machine and re-raises the exception at block exit instead of absorbing it, so the contracted VaultInactiveException raised by the checked deposit(5) at line 112 and withdraw(2) at line 115 still escapes TestVaultImplReal and the conformance test fails. low/vault.pyi contracts that deposit and withdraw on an inactive vault MUST raise VaultInactiveException, so the real-conformance test must expect that contracted exception with an actual catching assertion, such as self.assertRaises, around the checked calls at lines 112 and 115, and only then assert that the balance was left unchanged, while the active branch may assert increments and decrements.
[BLAME] benchmark_5/parts/inter_interface/pretense/inter_interface_impl_pretense.py: Reading the collaborator balance from the modeled pretense state fixed the earlier balance assertions, but two defects remain. The fuzzing fixture in lines 131-136 installs only the allocator in its lifecycle registry, so the real allocator cannot resolve its collaborator vault during fuzzing and InterInterfaceFuzzTest aborts with a lifecycle resolution error before any allocate or release contract is exercised; low/inter_interface_impl.pyi grounds the allocator in coordinating with the vault.Vault singleton, so the fixture must install the collaborator vault instance that matches the modeled collaborator state the pseudo-state machine inspects. In addition, the wrappers at lines 116 and 119 do not catch the exception: that seeding context re-raises the exception at block exit instead of absorbing it, so vault.VaultInactiveException still escapes TestInterInterfaceImplReal through the checked allocate(2) at line 117 and release(2) at line 120; the contracted exception must be expected with an actual catching assertion, such as self.assertRaises, followed by the unchanged-allocated assertions.
[CHANGE] benchmark_5/parts/inter_interface/pretense/vault_impl_pretense.py: Fixed feedback: TestVaultImplReal now uses unittest's catching assertion self.assertRaises(VaultInactiveException) around the checked deposit(5) and withdraw(2) on the inactive vault (the pretense raises context re-raises at block exit and does not absorb), then asserts the balance was left unchanged; the active branch still asserts increments/decrements.
[CHANGE] benchmark_5/parts/inter_interface/pretense/inter_interface_impl_pretense.py: Fixed feedback: make_sut now installs a blank pretense vault collaborator instance into the lifecycle registry under vault.Vault (the same modeled collaborator state sut_state(VaultState) inspects, and the collaborator VaultStateMachine drives), so the real allocator can resolve its collaborator during fuzzing instead of aborting on lifecycle resolution. TestInterInterfaceImplReal now expects the contracted vault.VaultInactiveException using a real catching assertion, self.assertRaises, for the inactive-vault allocate(2)/release(2), then asserts allocated is unchanged. Allocate/release overrides also gate on the inspected collaborator balance/allocated so unfunded fuzz draws cannot violate the collaborator precondition, while successful calls still assert the allocated and modeled vault balance postconditions.
