[BLAME] benchmark_5/parts/inter_interface/pretense/vault_pretense.py: The withdraw gate at lines 70-71 restricts amount to Domain.range(1, self.state.balance), an exclusive upper bound that rejects a withdrawal exactly equal to the modeled balance, so the legitimate full-balance withdraw(6) at the end of the real-conformance sequence fails domain validation and TestVaultImplReal aborts. low/vault.pyi defines a valid withdrawal as any positive amount that does not exceed the balance, treating only non-positive or above-balance amounts as InsufficientFundsError violations, so the argument domain must admit every value from 1 through the modeled balance inclusive; the current bound excludes the balance itself, making a full-balance withdrawal unreachable and leaving the successful decrement-to-zero postcondition unexercised, and it also leaves the boundary case where the modeled balance is 1 with no permitted amount at all.
[CHANGE] benchmark_5/parts/inter_interface/pretense/vault_pretense.py: Fixed feedback: withdraw argument domain now uses Domain.range(1, self.state.balance + 1) so the exclusive upper bound admits every valid amount from 1 through the modeled balance inclusive, including the full-balance withdraw(6) that decrements to zero and the balance==1 boundary case. The require(self.state.balance >= 1) gate still applies before the inactivity branch so no withdrawal is drawn at balance 0, keeping InsufficientFundsError unreachable during fuzzing.
